From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:09:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: smooth streaming from a playout buffer (MiaAI-Lab
 recipe patch 0061)

TF_GLM_STREAM_SMOOTH=1 sends a streamed reply's tokens one event each at a steady pace from a short playout buffer
(TF_GLM_STREAM_SMOOTH_MS, default 400 ms), so a drafted round's burst and a pause while the engine fills another
request's prompt are spread over the tokens already queued instead of showing as a freeze. Off unless set: unset or
0, the server writes exactly the events it wrote before (checked byte for byte on fixed fake engines).

- cuda/stream_pacing.py: the recipe's file whole (Playout, smooth_streaming, hold_seconds), two lines changed for
  lint (Callable from collections.abc, sorted __slots__), with the credit header.
- cuda/server.py App.run: send() through the playout, text_delta(), a multi-token round split into one event per
  token unless the round ends the reply (then the queue is flushed and the end is never later), the playout closed
  (or aborted when the client left) after generate. Written against this tree's server: #285's ToolCallStreamer
  call deltas follow their round's text unpaced, so a tool call keeps its place in the stream. Differences from the
  recipe: the playout and its writer thread are made just before the engine runs (a refused or cancelled request
  leaves no writer behind), and an engine failure sends the text still queued before the error, as unsmoothed (the
  recipe drops it).

Tests: tests/test_cuda_stream_smooth.py (the settings; Playout's pacing, hold bound, unpaced items in order, flush,
close, abort, a failed or raising write, a client gone; the server's SSE byte-identical with the setting unset for
text, thinking and tool-call engines, and with it on the same text token by token, the end not delayed, a tool call
in its place). With TF_GLM_STREAM_SMOOTH=1 the server, tool and stream test files pass as unset except
test_cuda_server_disconnect's timed-out write, which expects the engine to stop in the round whose write failed (the
writer thread finds the failure a few rounds later).

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("Smooth streaming") and the ported code's comments name MiaAI-Lab and the patch.

